    "share.title": "📊 Anonymous stats",
    "share.hint": "About once an hour while it runs, RigSweep sends what it cleaned since the last report, one entry per type with the time, the type and how much it freed; which well-known apps use the most CPU and memory; once a day, which hardware and driver software (from a fixed list of vendors such as ASUS, Dell, HP, NVIDIA or Logitech) is installed, whether it runs and how much it uses; your PC's RAM size and core count; the RigSweep version and Windows build. They feed the public counters on rigsweep.com and show what to improve next. Never sent: file paths, folder, project or process names (apart from well-known apps like Chrome or VS Code and that vendor software), user or PC names, hardware IDs. Your IP address is used only to look up the country and is never stored.",
